  "step_3": "The decision reason requires the individual to compute the mean difference between outcomes and the reference value (2400) and prefer the lottery with the higher mean difference. The individual did not compute any differences or expected values. Instead, the justification was based solely on the chance of getting more (i.e., 2500 Euros), which corresponds to the positive difference in Lottery B. While this reflects an awareness of the difference between outcomes and the reference value, the individual did not consider the full probabilistic structure—specifically, the negative difference of 2400 Euros with 1% probability, nor did they weigh it against the positive difference. The reason requires a calculation of the mean difference, which the individual did not perform. Therefore, although the individual considered the difference from the reference value (2400), they did not use the rule of comparing the expected (mean) differences. The justification is consistent with a heuristic focus on the possibility of a higher outcome, not the formal application of the mean difference rule. Thus, the decision reason was not used in the way specified.",
  "final_assessment_score": 30
}

